{"id": "section-body-00853", "title": "Approach to Altered Mental Status", "chapterId": "chapter-one", "blocks": [{"id": "body-00853", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading2", "text": "Approach to Altered Mental Status", "runs": [{"text": "Approach"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Altered"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Mental"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Status"}], "level": 2, "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1890"}}, {"id": "body-00854", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "This is the acute alteration in brain function and may include alteration of arousal or awareness, thought content, memory or attention.", "runs": [{"text": "This is the acute alteration in brain function and may include alteration of arousal or awareness, thought content,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "memory or "}, {"text": "attention."}]}, {"id": "body-00856", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Depending on the cause but may include agitation, Restlessness, Hemiparesis, visual deficit, dysphasia", "runs": [{"text": "Depending"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "on"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cause"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "but"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "include"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "agitation,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Restlessness,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Hemiparesis,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "visual"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "deficit,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dysphasia"}]}, {"id": "body-00857", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Differential diagnosis", "runs": [{"text": "Differential"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "diagnosis"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-00858", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "The mnemonic AEIOU TIPS is widely preferred in the emergency department when considering a broader differential. Alcohol/acidosis, Epilepsy/Electrolytes, Insulin/Inborn Errors of Metabolism, Oxygen/Overdose, Uremia, Trauma, Infection, Psychiatric/Poisoning, Stroke/Subarachnoid Hemorrhage/Shock", "runs": [{"text": "The mnemonic AEIOU TIPS is widely preferred in the emergency department when considering a broader differential. Alcohol/acidosis, Epilepsy/Electrolytes, Insulin/Inborn Errors of Metabolism, Oxygen/Overdose, Uremia, Trauma, Infection, Psychiatric/Poisoning, Stroke/Subarachnoid Hemorrhage/Shock"}]}, {"id": "body-00859", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Investigations", "runs": [{"text": "Investigations"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-00860", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "POC Glucose, Rapid Malaria test, Blood gases, Serum Electrolytes, POC ECG, Bedside ultrasound, Serum Creatinine and Urea, Lactate, Complete Blood Count, Liver function tests, Head CT-scan, Chest Xray and/or Toxicology screening (If highly suspicious of intoxication)", "runs": [{"text": "POC Glucose, Rapid Malaria test, Blood gases, Serum Electrolytes, POC ECG, Bedside ultrasound, Serum Creatinine and Urea,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Lactate,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Complete Blood Count,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Liver"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "function tests,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Head CT-scan,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Chest"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Xray and/or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Toxicology screening (If"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "highly suspicious of intoxication)"}]}, {"id": "body-00861", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Non- Pharmacological Management:", "runs": [{"text": "Non-"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Management:"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-00862", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "If aggressive/ restless, consider restraining- mechanical or chemical (medications)", "runs": [{"text": "If"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "aggressive/"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "restless,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "consider"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "restraining-"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mechanical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "chemical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(medications)"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1884"}}, {"id": "body-00863", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Obtain a set of vital signs, including random blood glucose", "runs": [{"text": "Obtain"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "set"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "vital"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "signs,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "including"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "random"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "blood"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "glucose"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1884"}}, {"id": "body-00864", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Perform both primary and secondary assessments and provide necessary interventions.", "runs": [{"text": "Perform"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "both"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "primary"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "secondary"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "assessments"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "provide"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "necessary"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "interventions."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1884"}}, {"id": "body-00865", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Give Oxygen if Hypoxic or dyspneic", "runs": [{"text": "Give"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Oxygen"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "if"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Hypoxic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dyspneic"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1884"}}, {"id": "body-00866", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Connect the patient to the cardiac monitor to obtain vital signs", "runs": [{"text": "Connect"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patient"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cardiac"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "monitor"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "obtain"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "vital"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "signs"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1884"}}, {"id": "body-00868", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Pharmacological Management", "runs": [{"text": "Pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Management"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-00869", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Treatment will depend on the cause of the altered mental status. For agitated patients, if needed to sedate, use: A: diazepam (IV): Adults 5-10mg loading dose, maintenance 0.03-0.1mg/kg every 30 minutes to 6 hours; Pediatrics 0.1-0.15mg/kg stat, may repeat after 3-5 minutes", "runs": [{"text": "Treatment will depend on the cause of the altered mental status. For agitated patients, if needed to sedate, use: "}, {"text": "A:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "diazepam"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(IV):"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Adults"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "5-10mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "loading"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dose,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "maintenance"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "0.03-0.1mg/kg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "every"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "30"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "minutes"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "6"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "hours; Pediatrics 0.1-0.15mg/kg stat, may repeat after 3-5 minutes"}]}, {"id": "body-00870", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Heading3", "text": "OR", "runs": [{"text": "OR"}], "level": 3, "conjunction": true}, {"id": "body-00871", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "B: haloperidol (IV): Adults 0.5-10mg (If concerned about psychiatric disorder) Child: safety and effectiveness not established", "runs": [{"text": "B: ", "bold": true}, {"text": "haloperidol (IV): Adults 0.5-10mg (If concerned about psychiatric disorder) Child: safety and effectiveness not "}, {"text": "established"}]}, {"id": "body-00872", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Heading3", "text": "OR", "runs": [{"text": "OR"}], "level": 3, "conjunction": true}, {"id": "body-00873", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "B: ketamine (IV) 1-2mg/kg and 2-4mg/kg for (IM)", "runs": [{"text": "B:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "ketamine"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(IV)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "1-2mg/kg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "2-4mg/kg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(IM)"}]}, {"id": "body-00874", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Heading3", "text": "OR", "runs": [{"text": "OR"}], "level": 3, "conjunction": true}, {"id": "body-00875", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "D: midazolam (IV): Adults 5mg stat, maintenance 20-100mcg/kg/hr. infusion; Pediatrics 0.05-0.1mg/kg stat.", "runs": [{"text": "D:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "midazolam"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(IV):"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Adults"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "5mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "stat,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "maintenance"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "20-100mcg/kg/hr."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "infusion;"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Pediatrics"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "0.05-0.1mg/kg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "stat."}]}, {"id": "body-00876-textbox1-00001", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Note: Consult/refer to a higher center with a psychiatrist if concerned about a psychiatric disorder", "runs": [{"text": "Note:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Consult/refer"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "higher"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "center"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "psychiatrist"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "if"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "concerned"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "about"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "psychiatric"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "disorder"}]}], "source": {"file": "medical.docx", "chapter": "Approach to patients with emergency conditions", "start": "body-00853", "end": "body-00876-textbox1-00001"}}